# Extra TLS certificate locations for Mail Archiver, one glob per line.
#
# install-tls-cert.sh searches these IN ADDITION to its built-in defaults
# (certbot, generic Debian/RHEL layouts, cockpit, OpenMediaVault) and picks
# the newest certificate that is CA-issued, unexpired, key-matched, and
# carries this host's FQDN in its SAN.
#
# Use this to support a platform we do not ship a rule for, without
# patching the script. Private keys are located automatically next to the
# certificate or in the usual private directories; if your layout is
# unusual, set MAIL_ARCHIVER_TLS_CERT and MAIL_ARCHIVER_TLS_KEY instead
# (an explicit pair always wins).
#
# Install to /etc/mail-archiver/tls-sources.conf
#
# Examples:
#/etc/ssl/mycompany/*.fullchain.pem
#/opt/vendor-appliance/pki/tls/server.crt
